<header class="en-head"><p class="en-eyebrow">HISTORY & CULTURE · ARGENTINA</p><h1>What Is a Gaucho? <em>Meaning, History, and Argentine Culture</em></h1><p class="en-intro">Long before the gaucho became a familiar emblem of Argentina, men worked with cattle and horses across the grasslands of the Río de la Plata. Their lives were shaped not just by independence and open country, but also by demanding labor, shifting laws, and unequal access to land.</p><p class="en-meta">MARTINFIERRO.ORG · Original English historical guide · Research-based editorial overview</p></header>
